{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Therefore you and all your assembly</b> – לָכֵן, because of this: you and all your assembly who are gathered against YHWH, for by His commission I acted to give the priesthood to Aaron, and this dispute is not ours – this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Numbers 16:11). And if so, the meaning is: you and all your assembly, you are the ones gathered against YHWH, not against Aaron. And Ibn Ezra said (Ibn Ezra on Numbers 16:11) that the letter ה in הַנּוֹעָדִים is superfluous. And it is possible to say: לָכֵן you and all your assembly who are gathered against YHWH – for they were not against Aaron – [come] before HaShem with Aaron tomorrow, and the verse is elliptical regarding the conditions that he mentioned. And the meaning of the verse is that at first he spoke to Korah and to all his assembly, saying: \"In the morning YHWH will make known\" etc., and afterward he turned to speak with Korah: \"You have gone too far, sons of Levi,\" and he said to Korah alone: \"Hear now, sons of Levi.\" Therefore he returned and said: \"You and all your assembly who are gathered against YHWH,\" for the punishment does not fall upon him alone, but upon all his assembly, for all of them are gathered against YHWH."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:05:59.646954613Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}